{"lines": ["Around three in the morning on the twenty-sixth of December, 1980, a security patrol near the east gate of RAF Woodbridge saw lights apparently descending into Rendlesham Forest, in Suffolk, England.", "The base was then used by the United States Air Force. The servicemen first thought an aircraft had come down.", "In the forest, a memo later said, they saw a glowing object that looked metallic, with coloured lights.", "In daylight, they found three small impressions in the ground, burn marks, and broken branches. Local police thought an animal could have made the marks.", "Two nights later, deputy base commander Lieutenant Colonel Charles Halt took a radiation meter to the site. The reading in the depressions was slightly higher than elsewhere, but the numbers stayed close to background level.", "Halt recorded the events on a micro-cassette, and wrote a memo to the UK Ministry of Defence.", "Sceptics explain the lights as a fireball, the Orfordness lighthouse, and bright stars. The Ministry stated the event posed no threat to national security.", "Both things are true. And because an officer filed a report, we can still read what was said.", "An official report puts a sighting on the record."], "words": [["Around", 0.0, 0.24], ["three", 0.24, 0.72], ["in", 0.72, 0.98], ["the", 0.98, 1.06], ["morning", 1.06, 1.42], ["on", 1.42, 1.78], ["the", 1.78, 1.88], ["twenty-sixth", 1.88, 2.72], ["of", 2.72, 2.78], ["December,", 2.78, 3.32], ["1980,", 3.32, 4.46], ["a", 5.34, 5.42], ["security", 5.42, 5.76], ["patrol", 5.76, 6.42], ["near", 6.42, 6.76], ["the", 6.76, 6.94], ["east", 6.94, 7.3], ["gate", 7.3, 7.6], ["of", 7.6, 7.9], ["RAF", 7.9, 8.2], ["Woodbridge", 8.2, 9.12], ["saw", 9.12, 9.6], ["lights", 9.6, 9.96], ["apparently", 9.96, 10.46], ["descending", 10.46, 10.92], ["into", 10.92, 11.54], ["Rendlesham", 11.54, 12.16], ["Forest,", 12.16, 12.64], ["in", 12.64, 13.12], ["Suffolk,", 13.12, 13.46], ["England.", 13.96, 14.16], ["The", 15.06, 15.2], ["base", 1